# Normalise line endings as a property of the repository rather than of each
# machine.
#
# Nothing is currently broken: everything here is committed LF, because both
# development machines happen to have core.autocrlf=true. That is a per-machine
# git setting, though, not something the repo enforces -- a contributor with
# autocrlf=false, or a fresh clone configured differently, can commit CRLF
# without noticing.
#
# The consequence is not cosmetic for this project. infra/*.sh run on the EC2
# box via GitHub Actions -> SSM, and bash fails on every line of a CRLF script
# with "$'': command not found" -- so it breaks the deploy rather than
# showing up as a diff someone reviews. Dockerfiles, docker-compose, systemd
# units and any .env read by `docker --env-file` (values gain a trailing )
# have the same failure mode.

* text=auto

# Executed on Linux — CRLF here is a runtime failure, not a formatting nit.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerignore  text eol=lf

# Parsed by tools that treat \r as part of the value.
*.env           text eol=lf
.env.*          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# Kept LF for consistent diffs across the two machines this is developed on.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.ini           text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.jsx           text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf
